import ConnesWeilRH.Source.CCM25Concrete.CCM24FiniteSCompletedJuliaRawPhysicalOldCarrierCoframeJointGapResponseReadout

/-!
# Antiresonant reduction of the old-carrier Bone 1 target

The response-facing Bone 1 contract contains a nonzero Schur--Markov scalar.
The first theorem below cancels that scalar and exposes the actual target:

```text
oldFrame * rawIntertwining = oldCarrierAnalysis^dagger * factor.
```

The old-carrier analysis has two physical coordinates.  On the new-frame
range, however, both coordinates are generated by the same ambient-loss
column.  More precisely,

```text
oldCarrierAnalysis * newFrame
  = newRangeAmbientLossLift * ambientLoss^dagger * newFrame.
```

The lift is uniformly bounded by `2`.  Thus the new-frame restriction of
Bone 1 is a genuine antiresonant divisibility problem for the single factor
`ambientLoss^dagger`, rather than a spectral-gap problem for the packed
analysis.  No divisibility or Gate 3U estimate is asserted here.
-/

